config LNET_GNILND
	tristate "Cray GNI LND (kgnilnd)"
	depends on LNET
	default n
	help
	  The gni LND (kgnilnd) carries LNet traffic over the Cray Gemini
	  and Aries high-speed networks using the GNI API. It requires the
	  Cray GNI kernel headers, so it is normally only built on Cray
	  systems.

	  To compile this as a kernel module, choose M here and it will be
	  called kgnilnd.

	  If unsure, say N.
